<ServicePage title="Appeal a Denied Disability Claim" description="Learn what may happen after Social Security denies an SSI or SSDI claim and how Williams & Swee, Ltd. may help." intro="Social Security denied your application. You may be able to ask Social Security to review that decision. This is called an appeal." points={['A denial is not always the end of your claim.','Appeals have deadlines, so read your notice promptly.','The next step may be reconsideration, a hearing, or another review.']} steps={['Find the denial notice and the date printed on it.','Do not start a new application unless you understand how it may affect your appeal.','Call the firm promptly to discuss the notice and possible deadline.']} />
